1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,103
Here is a question with a strange answer.

2
00:00:03,103 --> 00:00:06,051
When is the tyre valve
exactly at half height?

3
00:00:06,451 --> 00:00:09,324
Aarav watched it on his
bicycle wheel today.

4
00:00:09,324 --> 00:00:12,452
Half height means half
the radius above the hub.

5
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:14,470
At thirty degrees, yes.

6
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:18,393
At one hundred and fifty degrees,
on the way down, yes again.

7
00:00:18,793 --> 00:00:21,597
Then the wheel turns on
and does it all again.

8
00:00:21,597 --> 00:00:24,240
Three ninety, five ten, and on, forever.

9
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,953
One equation, endless answers.

10
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:29,856
Today we write all of them in one line.

11
00:00:29,856 --> 00:00:32,175
These are trigonometric equations.

12
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:35,404
So what is a trigonometric equation?

13
00:00:35,754 --> 00:00:40,557
It is an equation with a trigonometric
function of an unknown angle, like

14
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:42,341
sine x equals one half.

15
00:00:42,741 --> 00:00:47,541
The solutions from zero up to two pi,
one full turn, are called principal

16
00:00:47,541 --> 00:00:48,441
solutions.

17
00:00:48,761 --> 00:00:53,526
One formula, using an integer n, that
gives every solution, is called the

18
00:00:53,526 --> 00:00:54,742
general solution.

19
00:00:55,392 --> 00:00:57,406
Watch the solutions appear.

20
00:00:57,406 --> 00:01:01,477
Draw y equals sine x, and
the line y equals one half.

21
00:01:01,877 --> 00:01:05,498
Every time the wave crosses
the line, we get a solution.

22
00:01:05,498 --> 00:01:06,398
Count them.

23
00:01:06,772 --> 00:01:08,263
Two in the first turn.

24
00:01:08,263 --> 00:01:09,708
Two more in the next.

25
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:12,681
The wave never stops, so
neither do the answers.

26
00:01:13,331 --> 00:01:14,637
Now raise the line.

27
00:01:14,637 --> 00:01:17,632
Let the height k climb
from one half towards one.

28
00:01:18,032 --> 00:01:21,724
At k equals one, the line
only touches each hilltop.

29
00:01:21,724 --> 00:01:23,378
One solution per turn.

30
00:01:23,778 --> 00:01:27,058
Above one, the line misses
the wave completely.

31
00:01:27,058 --> 00:01:30,626
Sine x equals one point
two has no solution at all.

32
00:01:31,276 --> 00:01:34,548
Now let us build the general
solution, step by step.

33
00:01:34,898 --> 00:01:35,806
Step one.

34
00:01:35,806 --> 00:01:38,086
Say sine x equals sine alpha.

35
00:01:38,086 --> 00:01:39,680
One answer is easy.

36
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,986
x equals alpha.

37
00:01:41,736 --> 00:01:42,636
Step two.

38
00:01:42,527 --> 00:01:43,916
Sine is the height.

39
00:01:43,916 --> 00:01:48,199
The point at pi minus alpha has
the same height, so it works too.

40
00:01:48,949 --> 00:01:49,927
Step three.

41
00:01:49,927 --> 00:01:53,763
Each full turn of two pi
brings the same heights back.

42
00:01:53,763 --> 00:01:58,397
So x is two n pi plus alpha, or
two n pi plus pi minus alpha.

43
00:01:59,147 --> 00:02:00,118
Step four.

44
00:02:00,118 --> 00:02:01,257
Look closely.

45
00:02:01,257 --> 00:02:04,127
Even multiples of pi carry plus alpha.

46
00:02:04,127 --> 00:02:06,528
Odd multiples carry minus alpha.

47
00:02:07,278 --> 00:02:09,303
So one line holds them all.

48
00:02:09,303 --> 00:02:13,570
x equals n pi, plus minus one
to the power n, times alpha.

49
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,472
The same idea works for the others.

50
00:02:16,872 --> 00:02:22,342
cos is the across distance, and alpha
and minus alpha have the same across.

51
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:27,092
So cos x equals cos alpha gives
two n pi, plus or minus alpha.

52
00:02:27,492 --> 00:02:29,619
tan repeats every half turn.

53
00:02:29,619 --> 00:02:33,230
So tan x equals tan alpha
gives n pi plus alpha.

54
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:35,310
And two special ones.

55
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:38,298
Sine x is zero at every multiple of pi.

56
00:02:38,298 --> 00:02:42,137
cos x is zero at every odd
multiple of pi over two.

57
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:43,983
Side by side.

58
00:02:43,983 --> 00:02:46,930
Principal solutions live inside one turn.

59
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:52,258
For sine x equals one half, they are
pi over six and five pi over six.

60
00:02:52,658 --> 00:02:55,235
The general solution covers every turn.

61
00:02:55,235 --> 00:02:59,857
Put n equals two into the formula,
and you get thirteen pi over six.

62
00:03:00,457 --> 00:03:01,602
Now you try.

63
00:03:01,602 --> 00:03:04,917
Is thirteen pi over six
a principal solution?

64
00:03:04,917 --> 00:03:06,340
Pause and decide.

65
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,440
No!

66
00:03:09,964 --> 00:03:13,057
It is a solution, but it
is bigger than two pi.

67
00:03:13,057 --> 00:03:16,381
It lives in the second turn,
so it is not principal.

68
00:03:17,031 --> 00:03:18,086
Remember this.

69
00:03:18,086 --> 00:03:20,670
Find one answer, then add every turn.

70
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:23,105
Now, one worked example.

71
00:03:23,455 --> 00:03:26,896
Solve sine x equals minus
root three over two.

72
00:03:27,396 --> 00:03:28,296
Step one.

73
00:03:28,222 --> 00:03:31,342
Sine of pi over three
is root three over two.

74
00:03:31,342 --> 00:03:35,740
Sine is negative below the hub,
in the third and fourth quadrants.

75
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:37,410
Step two.

76
00:03:37,410 --> 00:03:43,207
So sine x equals sine of pi plus pi
over three, which is four pi over three.

77
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:44,917
Step three.

78
00:03:44,917 --> 00:03:49,824
The general solution is n pi, plus
minus one to the power n, times four

79
00:03:49,824 --> 00:03:51,003
pi over three.

80
00:03:51,753 --> 00:03:52,672
Step four.

81
00:03:52,672 --> 00:03:57,628
Inside one turn, that gives four pi
over three and five pi over three.

82
00:03:57,628 --> 00:04:00,005
These are the principal solutions.

83
00:04:00,755 --> 00:04:02,221
Now, the exam trap.

84
00:04:02,571 --> 00:04:04,768
Solve cos x equals one half.

85
00:04:04,768 --> 00:04:08,824
Many students write n pi,
plus or minus pi over three.

86
00:04:09,224 --> 00:04:10,712
Try n equals one.

87
00:04:10,712 --> 00:04:13,921
Four pi over three has cos minus one half.

88
00:04:13,921 --> 00:04:14,821
Wrong!

89
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:17,119
For cos, the turns are two pi.

90
00:04:17,119 --> 00:04:21,595
The right answer is two n pi,
plus or minus pi over three.

91
00:04:22,245 --> 00:04:23,831
Where is this asked?

92
00:04:23,831 --> 00:04:28,545
In JEE Main and JEE Advanced, as
questions that count the solutions in

93
00:04:28,545 --> 00:04:30,791
an interval, or add them up.

94
00:04:31,391 --> 00:04:32,669
Exam level now.

95
00:04:32,669 --> 00:04:35,626
How many solutions from zero to four pi?

96
00:04:35,626 --> 00:04:36,958
Pause and solve.

97
00:04:42,358 --> 00:04:43,650
The answer is C.

98
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:44,550
Six.

99
00:04:44,661 --> 00:04:47,003
Treat sine x as one unknown.

100
00:04:47,003 --> 00:04:52,584
The equation factorises as two sine
x minus one, times sine x minus one.

101
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:56,133
So sine x is one half, or sine x is one.

102
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:59,964
One half gives two
solutions per turn, so four.

103
00:04:59,964 --> 00:05:02,349
One gives one per turn, so two.

104
00:05:02,349 --> 00:05:03,357
Six in all.

105
00:05:03,957 --> 00:05:05,413
Here is your recap.

106
00:05:05,413 --> 00:05:06,910
Screenshot this card.

107
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:13,109
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

108
00:05:13,509 --> 00:05:14,409
One.

109
00:05:14,059 --> 00:05:17,891
Find the principal solutions
of cos x equals one half.

110
00:05:18,791 --> 00:05:19,691
Two.

111
00:05:19,344 --> 00:05:22,753
Write the general solution
of tan x equals one.

112
00:05:23,653 --> 00:05:24,553
Three.

113
00:05:24,261 --> 00:05:28,058
How many solutions does sine
x equals three over two have?

114
00:05:29,158 --> 00:05:32,105
Next time: x squared plus one equals zero.

115
00:05:32,105 --> 00:05:34,540
No number on the number line works.

116
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,884
So we need a new kind of number.

117
00:05:36,884 --> 00:05:38,060
Complex numbers.
